# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Root env — used by `sanity.blueprint.ts` (blueprint/function deploys).
# Copy this file to `.env` (not only `.env.local`) and fill in.
#
# Required alongside:
#   cp studio/.env.example studio/.env
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#
# Studio CLI loads studio/.env; blueprint loads this root `.env`.
# A root-only `.env.local` is not enough for `pnpm bootstrap`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your Sanity project ID and dataset (from sanity.io/manage)
SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID=
SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET=production

# ── Analytics sync (Phase 1: GitHub Actions cron / standalone script) ─────────
# A write-enabled token is only needed when running the sync outside the Studio
# CLI (e.g. in CI). `pnpm bootstrap`/`pnpm seed`/`pnpm analytics-sync` use your
# CLI login token instead. Create at: sanity.io/manage → API → Tokens (Editor).
# SANITY_API_WRITE_TOKEN=

# Which analytics provider the sync reads from. "fixture" ships deterministic
# demo data so the sync runs with no external credentials. Set to "ga4" to read
# from Google Analytics 4 (requires the GA4 vars below).
ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=fixture

# ── GA4 provider (only when ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=ga4) ───────────────────────────
# GA4 property ID, e.g. "properties/123456789"
# GA4_PROPERTY_ID=
# Base64-encoded service-account JSON with the Analytics Data API (read-only)
# GA4_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY=
